# The trial of pod-proxy in podnet: the way out of each connection
# (src/egress.rs), the HTTP client (src/fetch.rs) and the credentials of a
# served proxy take pod-proxy, with podnet's rules of the variables, its
# --proxy, its resolver chain, its counters, and its words and hops of a
# failure. The record, the size of the files, the build, the bans and the
# sources of cargo-deny, clippy, the tests of the library, the integration
# tests that read the way out, the fuzz targets with their lock, which
# follows the crates of the tree (at the tag, the consumer runs the same
# `cargo update -w` in fuzz/), and rustfmt.
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- remap Cargo.lock > /dev/null
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- check
python3 scripts/check-size.py
cargo build -q
command -v cargo-deny > /dev/null || cargo install -q --locked cargo-deny
cargo deny --locked check bans sources
cargo clippy -q --all-targets -p podnet -p podnet-netns -- -D warnings
cargo test -q -p podnet --lib
cargo test -q -p podnet --test egress --test tls --test relay_reverse --test cli --test doctor --test api_surface --test connect --test docs --test update_umask
cargo update -q -w --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml
cargo check -q --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml --bins
cargo fmt --all --check
